set.body:
Successor split from bd-01M23ZX1KQB38EPD7W3PM56SE9 after independent qualification of its deterministic max-null cutoff repair.

Scope:
- inventory implemented versus enum-only threshold methods and keep unavailable methods unadvertised;
- verify one-sided and two-sided orientation for observed and null fields;
- qualify Monte Carlo plus-one and exact-enumeration conventions and null-family identity;
- require common subject-bound null actions, fixed search masks, explicit missing or failed draws, and declared multiplicity families;
- establish the conditions needed for strong Westfall-Young step-down control;
- qualify adaptive HierScan regions and priors under the complete null;
- calibrate spatial FWER and FDR on prespecified complete-null and partial-null fields with spatial dependence, small n, heterogeneity, and supported first-level uncertainty;
- verify p-value, cutoff, mask, legend, native result, and consumer round-trip agreement;
- retain streaming max-null reduction and deterministic scheduling without a draws-by-voxels allocation.

Acceptance:
- predeclared protocols and independent oracles;
- fresh held-out calibration with every failed and unavailable case retained;
- JVM and Scala.js public API tests;
- source-bound consumer evidence;
- explicit method-by-method admission or refusal.

This successor does not reopen the repaired strict versus inclusive cutoff defect and does not treat that deterministic repair as spatial or statistical admission.
